# No scripted batch code edits

When implementing or fixing code, change source files with the editor (search-replace or writing the file). Do not run a script that rewrites source.

## Forbidden unless the developer explicitly allows it in this turn

- `node -e`, `python -c`, PowerShell, `sed`, or any other one-off script whose job is to splice, generate, or overwrite application source
- A script that walks the repo and rewrites many source files
- Shell command substitution that builds source text and writes it into a `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.sql`, `.json`, or `.md` file

## Allowed

- Editor edits to the files being changed
- One-shot commands that do not rewrite source: tests, `tsc`, git status, formatting the developer already uses
- A script the developer asked for as the deliverable itself (a tool they want to keep)

If a mechanical rewrite looks necessary, ask first. Do not start it and clean up afterwards.
